<Prose title="Privacy policy · GitHub Reskin" heading="Privacy policy" description="GitHub Reskin collects no data. What stays in your browser, embedded images and advanced CSS, and how to clear it." path="privacy/" lede="Sideband Studio. Last updated November 8, 2026.">
  <p>GitHub Reskin changes GitHub and Gist appearance using bundled themes or locally imported theme files. Themes may contain embedded raster images and optional advanced CSS. The extension and userscript do not collect or send data to Sideband Studio. They have no telemetry, analytics, advertising or data-collection server. They make no network requests of their own, including theme, font, analytics or AI service requests.</p>
  <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
  <p>Themes and preferences stay in local extension storage. This includes your selected theme, enabled state, Full/Calm and other display choices, saved themes with embedded raster images and sanitized CSS, and records of your approval to enable imported CSS. GitHub Reskin also keeps a recoverable editor draft, import text while you work on it, and limited recovery information. A theme may include a name, optional author credit, flavor text and images that you select. Those images or text may contain personal information.</p>
  <p>The extension uses browser-local extension storage, not browser sync. The userscript uses your userscript manager's local storage when that capability is available. Their settings are separate. A manager without persistent storage can offer a session preview and export instead.</p>
  <p>GitHub Reskin reads the current GitHub or Gist page's color-mode attributes, route and limited page structure to apply appearance, identify permitted CSS targets and place eligible decoration. It does not save a browsing-history log, record your typing, or extract a copy of your repositories, messages or comments. It does not ask for your GitHub password or token. A theme can change the font used to display prose, but it does not change or save that prose.</p>
  <h2>Imported files and AI prompts</h2>
  <p>When you select a theme file or paste a theme, GitHub Reskin reads and checks it locally. It does not upload the file, filename, import text or GitHub page to Sideband Studio or an AI service. Imported theme values and an unfinished import may remain in local saved themes or the recoverable draft until you replace or clear them.</p>
  <p>The AI prompt is text you choose to copy. It describes the theme format, including backgrounds, bundled fonts, code colors and optional CSS; it contains no GitHub page content or user identity and asks for no images. GitHub Reskin does not connect to a chatbot. If you paste the prompt, an image or other material into a chatbot, that service handles what you submit under its own terms and privacy policy. You choose what to send there.</p>
  <p>Fonts, effects, built-in themes and the CSS parser are included with the extension or userscript. They are not fetched from a font service or theme server.</p>
  <h2>Embedded images and advanced CSS</h2>
  <p>An imported theme can carry PNG, JPEG, WebP or GIF data for a wallpaper, profile banner or header. The local image chooser reads only the file you select. Reskin checks size and dimensions before decoding, converts accepted images locally to static PNG/WebP and strips metadata before persistence. Animated inputs become one frame. It never loads theme images from web URLs, and it rejects SVG. The converted image stays in the theme and local draft or saved collection until you replace or delete it. There is no image-analysis or upload service.</p>
  <p>A bundled parser rejects unsupported CSS and external resources. Reskin validates CSS locally, generates restricted styles for supported GitHub elements, and retains the original import only in the bounded recovery draft. It does not accept scripts, remote stylesheets, remote fonts or outside image resources as theme capabilities.</p>
  <p>Imported CSS is previewed and enabled explicitly. A theme containing it carries an Advanced CSS label, a source view and a warning that it can break layout or reduce readability. Approval is tied to the sanitized CSS and sanitizer version; changing the CSS requires a fresh choice. Built-in CSS uses the same sanitizer. Calm disables custom CSS and decorative images/effects. Calm does not delete the saved image, CSS or approval record.</p>
  <h2>Exporting and sharing</h2>
  <p>Downloading JSON or copying a share code does not upload a theme to Sideband Studio. Exported files and share codes include their embedded images and CSS, along with theme values, author credits and flavor text. Anyone given a file, code or complete preview link can extract those contents. Review personal images before sharing. Share codes are not encrypted. Local CSS approvals are not transferable consent; recipients must review and enable imported CSS themselves.</p>
  <p>Custom preview links put the theme in the part of the URL after #. The showcase page reads that part locally; the browser does not include it in the page's HTTP request. A recipient or the service you use to send the full link can still read it. If the complete URL would exceed 8192 characters, Reskin offers file export instead. Opening a preview link does not change an installed extension or enable CSS automatically.</p>
  <h2>Clearing local data</h2>
  <p>Delete an individual custom theme or use Reset all in GitHub Reskin's settings to clear saved settings, custom themes, embedded images, CSS, approval records, drafts and recovery records. An unfinished draft can retain an imported original until you clear or replace that draft. Export anything you want to keep first. Turning the extension off or choosing Calm retains saved data.</p>
  <p>Removing the extension normally removes its extension-managed storage according to your browser's behavior. For the userscript, remove the script and its stored values through the manager. Exported files, copied codes, links, browser backups and copies you sent to other people are separate; delete those where they are stored.</p>
  <p>Older versions stored generated styling under the github-reskin-css key in GitHub's and Gist's own site storage. The relaunch removes that key when you visit each site and does not store new themes there. An old copy on an unvisited site can remain after uninstalling. To remove it, use your browser's site-data controls for github.com and gist.github.com. Clearing a site's data can also sign you out and remove that site's preferences.</p>
  <h2>Websites, stores and support</h2>
  <p>GitHub and Gist, browser extension stores and their update services, and your userscript manager operate separately. A manager may check the published script URL for updates. Their network requests are not requests made by the theme script.</p>
  <p>The showcase and privacy pages are hosted on GitHub Pages. Visiting them sends ordinary web requests to the host. The showcase uses its bundled assets and has no analytics or theme-upload service. GitHub's handling of hosted-page requests follows <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>
  <p>Support is through <a href="https://github.com/sidebandstudio/GitHub-Reskin/issues">GitHub Issues</a>. If you open an issue, GitHub hosts what you submit and Sideband Studio uses it to investigate and answer your request. Issues are public. Include only information you want to publish. Support information you deliberately send is separate from automatic extension data collection.</p>
  <p>The repository also includes an optional contribution-graph GitHub Action. It runs in your GitHub Actions workflow, uses the GitHub API and writes an SVG to your repository. It is separate from the browser extension and its no-network behavior. Its output and workflow logs follow your repository's visibility and GitHub's practices.</p>
  <h2>Limited use and changes</h2>
  <p>GitHub Reskin's use of information complies with the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including its Limited Use requirements. We do not sell information or use it for advertising, unrelated purposes, or creditworthiness and lending decisions.</p>
  <p>We will date policy updates here and disclose changes in extension data handling before introducing them.</p>
  <p>For a question about this policy, open a <a href="https://github.com/sidebandstudio/GitHub-Reskin/issues">GitHub issue</a>.</p>
</Prose>
